{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KNXNbfX245P2jhmtdpUZL2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intervals.icu workout_doc API step hr target units %lthr bpm Garmin export zone\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/incorrect-structured-workout-rendering-in-calendar-export/127096\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"Workout Builder: Duration types\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder-duration-types/69924\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"Custom Heart Rate range planned workout\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/custom-heart-rate-range-planned-workout/72460\"}]\n\nThe search turned up forum posts and a community syntax guide, but no official schema listing every `units` value for HR steps.\n\n- **HR targets are stored as % of LTHR, not bpm.** A user reports that the target HR is sent as % of LTHR, and a Intervals.icu developer's explanation is that sending as % LTHR is done so that workouts can be exchanged with other users. Another user notes that the HR range needs to be given in % of threshold HR for portability.\n- **Absolute bpm targets aren't a native option.** One forum thread asks about a fixed bpm range and is told to convert it to a percentage of threshold HR, with an example of 130/170 ≈ 76% (\"- 10m 74-76% HR\"). Another user says they couldn't get bpm ranges to work in the editor.\n- **The workout_doc JSON uses a `units` field.** The API example for power shows a step with \"units\": \"power_zone\", and a fixed-power example uses \"units\": \"%ftp\". The HR analogue would presumably be `%lthr`, but I didn't find a source confirming that exact string.\n- **Ranges are added automatically.** Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range. For HR it is 1.5% by default, and this can be changed with an `hrRange` query parameter, where 0.0 disables the range (You can also supply powerRange, hrRange and paceRange query parameters to the call).\n- **Garmin export mismatches.** One user reported that workouts pulled from Garmin Connect showed bpm zones off by exactly 100 bpm in Intervals.icu. The thread suggests this comes from LTHR or zone settings differing between the two platforms, but it was never confirmed.\n- **Text syntax.** A community syntax guide shows HR-style targets are written with a `%` followed by `HR` (for example `74-76% HR`), but it covers power and cadence syntax in detail and doesn't document HR units.\n\nFor the authoritative `units` enum and the Garmin export behavior, the official Intervals.icu API docs or a test export would be the next place to check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4884390f-5ebe-4027-8722-59be6f14e314","uuid":"94fa50f9-9cec-43cf-ab0d-77a8bf22e893","timestamp":"