{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4j8f5r3p2rcoddNY5y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1806,"cache_read_input_tokens":26819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1806},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4884390f-5ebe-4027-8722-59be6f14e314","uuid":"8aeae993-3022-456e-bd5f-7dee4baec0c5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:53:37.771Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4j8NxUu1NuGst5teXr","thinking_duration_ms":304,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4j8f5r3p2rcoddNY5y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AUJtWw2KVH2MStmKdM1NsH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-dZkW6X/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: HR targets clamped to the watch's zones\n\n## What changed\n\n`gen.py`, `build_step()`: when a step has `hr_pct`, the output now sets\n`\"target\": \"HR\"` alongside the `hr` object. Nothing else changed.\n\nRegenerating `plans/tempo-run.json` now produces the same payload as\n`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json` plus four `\"target\": \"HR\"` lines, one per\nHR step (the warm-up, both tempo/float steps inside the repeat, and cool-down).\n\n## Why\n\nThe sent payload had an `hr` object with `units: \"%lthr\"` but no step-level\ntarget type. Intervals.icu's workout model keys each step's target by type\n(`HR`, `POWER`, `PACE`), and without it the step has no explicit HR target.\nThe watch then shows Garmin's zone-band target instead of the planned corridor,\nwhich matches what `readback/watch-notes.md` reports: every planned range\ncame back as a zone edge (118–137, 151–162, 137–151), and changing LTHR only\nmoved the bands.\n\n## What I could not verify\n\n- **The fix is not confirmed on the watch.** I did not push anything. Pushing or\n  checking the event against the live API would be an external action, and the\n  brief was to fix the generator only. The next step is to push a regenerated\n  event (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`),\n  re-sync, and check the displayed ranges against 117–129 / 151–160 / 129–141 / 112–124.\n- **I could not confirm the `units` enum.** A web search did not turn up the\n  official schema for HR `units` or how Intervals exports `%lthr` targets to\n  Garmin. If the watch still shows zone bands after the `target` fix, the\n  remaining suspect is the export mapping of `%lthr` ranges to Garmin zone\n  targets. The earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt produced 214–249 bpm, which\n  suggests those values were computed incorrectly. Recomputing bpm from LTHR\n  (`round(172 * pct / 100)`) in `gen.py` is the fallback to try, but it needs\n  checking against the API output before it is trusted.\n- The `start_bpm` / `end_bpm` attempt is not something this generator emits, so\n  it is not addressed here.\n\n## Files\n\n- `gen.py`: added `\"target\": \"HR\"` for steps with `hr_pct`.\n- `ANSWER.md`: this note.\n\nNothing was committed, pushed, or sent to any external service.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1806,"cache_read_input_tokens":26819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1806},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4884390f-5ebe-4027-8722-59be6f14e314","uuid":"62c81b6a-d19f-4ea1-a3e6-8fa571141ed8","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:53:41.471Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4j8NxUu1NuGst5teXr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AUJtWw2KVH2MStmKdM1NsH":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-dZkW6X/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: HR targets clamped to the watch's zones\n\n## What changed\n\n`gen.py`, `build_step()`: when a step has `hr_pct`, the output now sets\n`\"target\": \"HR\"` alongside the `hr` object. Nothing else changed.\n\nRegenerating `plans/tempo-run.json` now produces the same payload as\n`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json` plus four `\"target\": \"HR\"` lines, one per\nHR step (the warm-up, both tempo/float steps inside the repeat, and cool-down).\n\n## Why\n\nThe sent payload had an `hr` object with `units: \"%lthr\"` but no step-level\ntarget type. Intervals.icu's workout model keys each step's target by type\n(`HR`, `POWER`, `PACE`), and without it the step has no explicit HR target.\nThe watch then shows Garmin's zone-band target instead of the planned corridor,\nwhich matches what `readback/watch-notes.md` reports: every planned range\ncame back as a zone edge (118–137, 151–162, 137–151), and changing LTHR only\nmoved the bands.\n\n## What I could not verify\n\n- **The fix is not confirmed on the watch.** I did not push anything. Pushing or\n  checking the event against the live API would be an external action, and the\n  brief was to fix the generator only. The next step is to push a regenerated\n  event (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`),\n  re-sync, and check the displayed ranges against 117–129 / 151–160 / 129–141 / 112–124.\n- **I could not confirm the `units` enum.** A web search did not turn up the\n  official schema for HR `units` or how Intervals exports `%lthr` targets to\n  Garmin. If the watch still shows zone bands after the `target` fix, the\n  remaining suspect is the export mapping of `%lthr` ranges to Garmin zone\n  targets. The earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt produced 214–249 bpm, which\n  suggests those values were computed incorrectly. Recomputing bpm from LTHR\n  (`round(172 * pct / 100)`) in `gen.py` is the fallback to try, but it needs\n  checking against the API output before it is trusted.\n- The `start_bpm` / `end_bpm` attempt is not something this generator emits, so\n  it is not addressed here.\n\n## Files\n\n- `gen.py`: added `\"target\": \"HR\"` for steps with `hr_pct`.\n- `ANSWER.md`: this note.\n\nNothing was committed, pushed, or sent to any external service.\n"}}}
